      <h1 id="about-title" class="info-title"><span aria-hidden="true">$</span> About</h1>
      <p>Hello, I'm Riccardo, a Full Stack Web Developer, Systems Engineer, AI Engineer, and Coach.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="info-section" aria-labelledby="about-story">
      <h2 id="about-story"><span aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span> From games to the web</h2>
      <p>Like many nerdy kids who grew up in the '90s, I started writing code with the dream of making video games. I began with tools like RPG Maker 95 and GameMaker, but it didn't take long before I wanted more control over what I was building. That curiosity led me to C++, Ruby, and later C# - back when I was scripting custom mods for Ultima Online with RunUO. Good old days...</p>
      <p>I eventually found my way into web development because I needed websites for my own projects. I started with simple HTML, moved on to installing and modifying PHP-based CMSs and forums, and eventually built my first CMS entirely from scratch in PHP.</p>
      <p>Over time, I started earning my first money through web development, and from that point on, it became my main professional path. I grew into a full-stack developer, working across the entire stack - from server infrastructure and backend systems all the way to frontend development and UI.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="info-section" aria-labelledby="about-today">
      <h2 id="about-today"><span aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span> How I work today</h2>
      <p>Today, I combine everything I've learned over the years with an AI-first approach to software development, allowing me to work with a high level of speed and productivity. I specialize in agentic integration across business processes, software development, and DevOps.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="info-section" aria-labelledby="about-mentoring">
      <h2 id="about-mentoring"><span aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span> Mentoring and coaching</h2>
      <p>Over the years, I also realized that one of my greatest passions is helping people. So I decided to build on my experience as a developer by earning a degree in psychology and training as a coach.</p>
      <p>Today, I help IT professionals achieve their career and productivity goals, while also working with companies and managers to build healthy, productive work environments and teams.</p>
    </section>
